# TEST: gas + body axial momentum conservation in an axisymmetric domain
# x-periodic box, drifting gas, body of revolution initially at rest
# total x momentum = m_N * fnum * sum(vx) + M * vcm_x must be conserved
# as the gas pushes the body along the axis
#
# as in in.test.momentum, the exactly conserved quantity includes the
# half-step impulse 0.5*dt*fcm which velocity Verlet has in flight at
# any instant, so the invariant holds to round-off rather than to the
# statistical size of one step's transfer
#
# only the axial component is conserved: the radial and azimuthal
# momentum of the gas is not a conserved quantity of the axisymmetric
# model at all, since a particle's own (vy,vz) are rotated into the
# plane at every move, and the body by construction only responds to
# the azimuthal average of what the gas gives it
#
# run in both remap modes: the incremental re-cut must reproduce the
# full rebuild exactly, which for an axisymmetric domain also pins down
# the annular cell volumes it installs for cells the body vacates

seed	    	    12345

variable            dist index 0
variable            remap index incremental
if "${dist} == 1" then "global surfs explicit/distributed"
dimension   	    2
boundary            p ar p

create_box  	    0 1 0 0.3 -0.5 0.5
create_grid 	    20 6 1

global		    nrho 1.0 fnum 0.001

species		    air.species N
mixture		    air N vstream 100.0 0 0 temp 273.0

read_surf           adata.cylinder group body
surf_collide	    1 specular
surf_modify         all collide 1

timestep 	    1.0e-5


global              rigid yes

fix		    1 rigid body single body &
		    mass 1.0e-22 com 0.5 0 0 vcom 0 0 0 &
		    moi 5.0e-25 1.0e-24 1.0e-24 0 0 0 angmom 0 0 0 &
                    remap ${remap}

create_particles    air n 20000

variable px particle vx
compute r reduce sum v_px

stats		    200
stats_style         step np c_r f_1[4] f_1[7] f_1[8] f_1[9] f_1
stats_modify        format float %20.14e
run 		    2000
